#: ../content/index.rst:12
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:13
msgid "The Otobo OAuth2 packages adds support for OpenID Connect based authentication for incoming and outgoing webservice calls via Otobo's GenericInterface."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:16
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:17
msgid "With the Otobo OAuth2 package, webservice authentication using an OpenID Connect (OICD) provider can be enabled and configured. Otobo then can use OAuth2 tokens from your OICD provider to make authenticated outgoing webservice calls (GenericInterface Invokers), or validate such OAuth2 tokens for incoming webservice calls (GenericInterface Provider)."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:20
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:22
msgid "Use this package if"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:24
msgid "you are using an OpenID Connect (OIDD) Provider for Identity Management like MS Azure, Google, or a self hosted solution like keycloak."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:26
msgid "you want to use OIDC token based authentication for outgoing or incoming webservice calls using Otobo's GenericInterface"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:28
msgid "This packages is *not* needed if you are just looking for using OIDC as a login mechanism for Otobo. Login via OIDC is already built into Otobo core."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:31
msgid "Common Usecases"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:33
msgid "Usecase scenarios for this package include integration topics utilizing API communication via webservices, called GenericInterface in Otobo."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:35
msgid "Make Otobo provide webservice API endpoints to fetch Data from Otobo, authenticated using OAuth2 bearer tokens from your OIDC provider. Example: *GetTicket endpoint*"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:37
msgid "Make Otobo provide webservice API endpoints to call Otobo operations, authenticated using OAuth2 bearer tokens from your OIDC provider. Example: *UpdateTicket endpoint*"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:39
msgid "Make Otobo invoke other system's webservice API endpoints, passing data from the event trigger to the external system, and (possibly) doing something with whatever data returned, authenticated using OAuth2 bearer tokens from your OIDC provider. Example: *Pass Ticket data to remote system whenever ticket is updated.*"
msgstr ""

