#: ../content/index.rst:213
msgid "Setup User and Role Mapping for the OIDC Provider, and configure your OIDC provider to attach all necessary claims - most importantly probably 'roles' - to the issued access_tokens."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:215
msgid "or"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:217
msgid "Manually create an Agent in the Admin UI. For the access_token mapping to succeed, make sure you set the 'User Login' property in Otobo to the OIDC claim configured"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:219
msgid "in the `$Self->{'AuthModule::OpenIDConnect::UID'} = 'sub';` in Config.pm. The default shown here is mapping the 'sub' claim from the access_token to the Otobo user login."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:223
msgid "Provider Restrictions (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:225
msgid "Every valid Token needs to be mapped to a system user. If an API system user does not exist for an incoming webservice call, it will be created provided the Token passes validation, the Token contains roles, a corresponding Role Mapping exists, and the (optional) further restrictions you can configure in Otobo:"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:228
msgid "To add restrictions which valid tokens are accepted for incoming webservice calls, restrict by these fields in Config.pm:"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:230
msgid "``UserLogin``: only accept tokens of this particular login. This must match the UserLogin value in the Otobo System (UserLogin attribute of the User entity)."
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:232
msgid "``Scope``: a space separated list listing token's 'scope' claims that must be present in incoming tokens to be allowed"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:234
msgid "``Audience``: a space separated list listing token's 'aud' claims that must be present in incoming tokens to be allowed"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:236
msgid "``AuthorizedParty``: simple identifier that must match the token's 'azp' claim to be allowed"
msgstr ""

#: ../content/index.rst:238
msgid "Usually, you would either restrict to a specific user login, or to a combination of the other values, depending on your needs."
msgstr ""

